<script>
import Code from '#src/lib/Code.abide'
import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'
</script>

<Doc
    seeAlso={[
        '/app/on-launcher',
        '/native-app/on-menu',
        '/native-app/pending-update',
        '/request/is-server',
    ]}
    tests={[
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/native.test.ts',
            from: ["test('native() answers per request, and nothing outside one"],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/launcher.test.ts',
            from: ["test('a press on the titlebar drags and a double press zooms"],
        },
    ]}
>
    <Section level={3} title="Show a print button in a browser and not in the native window">
        <p><code>native()</code> answers the window's version and name, and
            <code>undefined</code> in a browser. The server reads the same answer from the
            request, so the button is never drawn in the window and taken away.</p>
        <Code language="abide" caption="abide" code={`
            <script>
            import { native } from '@abide/abide'
            </script>

            {#if !native()}
                <button onclick={() => window.print()}>Print report</button>
            {/if}
        `} />
        <p>Any client can send that user agent, so let it decide what a page shows, never who
            may do what.</p>
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Drag the window by a header drawn under its controls">
        <p>With <code>titlebar: 'inset'</code> in <code>onLauncher</code>, the page is drawn
            under the window's controls. Mark the element a press drags by, and keep clear of
            the controls with the two custom properties.</p>
        <Code language="abide" caption="abide" code={`
            <header
                data-abide-titlebar
                class="h-(--abide-titlebar-height) ps-(--abide-titlebar-inset)"
            >
                CRM
            </header>
        `} />
    </Section>
</Doc>
